WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:08.770
KEVIN JULIAN: Hello, and
welcome to our session

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.490
covering breakthrough insights
across the life sciences value

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.600
chain.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.870
I'm Kevin Julian,
senior managing director

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.600
in Accenture's life
sciences practice.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.080
And later I'll be joined by
my colleague, Mike Stapleton,

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.590
who's the head of strategy
for Accenture's life sciences

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.620
INTIENT platform.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.630
During this session,
we'll be talking

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.890
about why creating breakthrough
insights in life sciences

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.290
is more important than ever.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.350
And we'll share how INTIENT,
Accenture's life sciences

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.490
platform powered by Google, is
able to generate insights using

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.097
leading-edge Google technology.

00:00:47.097 --> 00:00:49.680
During this session, we'll spend
most of the time illustrating

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.440
examples of how insights are
being generated by INTIENT

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.240
across the life sciences
value chain, from earlier

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.580
research through
pivotal clinical trials

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.830
all the way through to
delivering care to patients.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.850
Our industry is at
a turning point,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.030
shifting from small
molecule, large population

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.620
strategic approaches to a more
targeted scientific approach.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:21.640
This shift is powered by what
we Accenture call New Science.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.370
New Science is a novel
chemistry or biology

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.270
in previously unsolved
areas of need,

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.970
like cell and gene therapy,
often enabled by technology

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.680
to deliver the
therapy or to support

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.520
the patient, or sometimes
maybe technology

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.940
itself, an app or other
technology solution

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.430
that intervenes in
an effective way

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.040
to improve the
patient [INAUDIBLE]..

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.510
Why the shift?

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.070
Something had to change.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.680
The old model simply
was not supporting

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.470
the needs of the market.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.560
New Science is attracting
significantly more attention

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.930
and investment, and
for good reason.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.380
Accenture Research is determined
that New Science therapies are

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.410
almost 50% more
likely to be approved

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:10.789
and greater than 50% of sales
over the next several years

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:15.110
are expected from New Science.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.160
This shift to New Science
brings the industry's dependence

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.290
on technology to the fore.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.500
Increasingly, industry
depends on connecting data

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.800
across the enterprise
to generate insights

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.560
into how therapies should
be developed and brought

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.240
to patients.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.910
While this ambition is
clear, it's also clear

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.910
that industry has yet to take
the necessary actions needed

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.320
to achieve their goal.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.670
According to this IDC study,
more than 50% of respondents

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:49.050
did not have a clear path to
connect, share, and analyze

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.210
information across
their organization.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:55.700
This is where INTIENT comes in.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.840
INTIENT, Accenture's platform
for the life sciences industry,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.130
powered by Google Cloud, enables
insights and collaboration

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:08.600
across the life
sciences enterprise.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.420
INTIENT helps the industry
generate breakthrough insights

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.210
in three powerful ways--

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.880
through functionally
oriented product suites

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.980
that have been built in
key areas of insight need--

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:26.980
drug research, clinical
trials, pharmacol vigilance,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.300
and patient services--

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.020
with other use cases enabled
by the INTIENT core platform,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.260
and through additional use cases
enabled by the INTIENT network,

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.990
our open ecosystem
access solution.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.770
Through access to innovative
specialty software, services,

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:48.190
hardware content, and
other business partners,

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:51.405
the INTIENT network offers
industry-standard APIs

00:03:51.405 --> 00:03:53.860
for pretty competitive
functions that

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.500
easily and quickly integrate
into existing systems.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.790
The ability to rapidly
and flexibly deploy

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.850
solutions and lower
barrier to entry

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:07.930
for new, small, and/or
niche software players--

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.810
all of this is made possible
by the INTIENT core platform

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.940
powered by Google Cloud.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.670
The core platform is a
flexible and powerful

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.839
data-centric solution
that connects

00:04:17.839 --> 00:04:20.470
a variety of data
sources and makes

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.090
insight generation possible.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.188
How does it do that?

00:04:25.188 --> 00:04:26.730
We start by using
Google's Healthcare

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.610
API to accelerate
solution development

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.830
and access third-party
solutions with fully

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:37.880
managed enterprise scale,
FHIR, HL7, and DICOM API.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.220
We use Google's
BigQuery to analyze

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.260
virtually unlimited
amounts of data

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:48.040
using standard SQL at scale
with zero operational overhead.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.580
And AutoML provides
non-expert users with access

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.940
to pre-configured, high-quality
machine learning models,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.100
such as image
detection, translation,

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.810
and natural language processing.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.680
Let's illustrate the power of
