on us and society in general.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:44.200
So let's start with research and
the fundamental challenges that

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.990
face drug discovery scientists.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.460
Whether they're
starting with a disease

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.570
or starting with a target
or starting with a biomarker

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:57.220
discovery program, or, indeed,
repurposing existing research

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:00.340
efforts, in every
single case, drug

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.470
discovery scientists
are challenged,

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:06.820
bringing together a wide
range of external data, lots

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:11.320
of historic, hard-to-retrieve
internal data,

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.710
assembling that data, bringing
it together in a format

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.550
that can be easily
managed, easily visualized,

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:22.690
and decisions taken from
that aggregated data.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.830
Consistently across the whole
of drug discovery research,

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.620
that integration of
data, that thinking

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.820
through a single query, how
easy it is to make a decision,

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.400
and how we can embed
advanced tools--

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.280
artificial intelligence,
machine learning--

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:42.310
so that more informed decisions,
more informed predictions

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:48.565
can be made to advance faster
and in a more focused way.

00:06:48.565 --> 00:06:50.190
To bring this to
life, I'm going to dig

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.200
into one of these
in a bit more detail

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.600
and take a look at
target discovery

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.150
as a particular example
to show the power

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.910
of the INTIENT platform.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.160
The key challenge here,
quite easy to state,

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.760
is that as an
industry, as a society,

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.480
we know more and more
about human disease biology

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.830
than we ever have done.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:14.970
And we continue to learn more
and more on a daily basis.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:19.470
Through the advances in
genomics to the connectivity

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.890
and measurements of mobile
devices that we all wear today,

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.930
we understand more
and more about us

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:28.530
as patients and how
that information

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:32.790
is connected to a therapeutic
or a particular condition

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:36.060
or a lifestyle that we
have as individuals.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.650
But even with that, yet
roughly 90% of candidate drugs

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:43.080
fail in the clinic.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.590
And a large number of those
fail because in early-stage drug

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.640
discovery, we still
choose poor targets.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.940
This has the obvious
consequences to the industry--

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:57.270
long development
times, increased cost,

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:02.820
and, quite significantly,
negative patient outcomes.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:05.510
So if we have the opportunity,
as we do with a platform

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.940
strategy like INTIENT, to
address this key bottleneck,

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.960
this key area of
pharmaceutical R&amp;D,

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:15.690
we would, quite clearly,
have huge impact.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.360
So why is it so difficult?

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.940
Let's have a look at the
operational consequences

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.950
of drug discovery today.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:24.170
Very diverse skill
sets are required

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:29.000
to manually bring together that
external and internal data.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.100
Integration of that data
is extremely time consuming

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:34.689
and often error-prone.

00:08:34.689 --> 00:08:38.860
Key patterns, key
indications, key predictions

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.590
can only be made
through machine learning

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:44.169
and artificial
intelligence capabilities,

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:46.810
not by the human mind.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.090
And so that's where the
INTIENT solution comes in.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:54.710
We can use the INTIENT solution
to bring in those broad array

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:55.760
of data sources.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.660
We can aggregate those data
sources, filter, pre-process,

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.860
and present the data in a much
more meaningful and accessible

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:09.320
way to a scientist, through
dashboards, alerts, predictions

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.150
that allow scientists to better
prioritize, better guide,

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:17.450
and allow a portfolio
activity of project teams

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:21.500
to better manage assets and to
move forward through the drug

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:26.510
discovery process, ultimately
identifying novel targets

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.330
and prioritizing
targets which have

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.210
a much higher
probability of success

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.953
further into
pharmaceutical development.

00:09:34.953 --> 00:09:36.620
Let's take a look at
a screenshot of how

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.320
that would actually look.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:43.460
And we see here a simple screen
shot of a modern user interface

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.710
from INTIENT, where
we bring together

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:51.210
that drill-down of
both therapy, genome,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.660
